{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 1, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJapan. The word itself conjures images of neon lights, ancient temples, and steaming bowls of ramen. And let me tell you, the reality is even more captivating. I just returned from a whirlwind trip and I'm already dreaming of going back.\n\nMy journey started in Tokyo, a city that assaults your senses in the best possible way. Shibuya Crossing was an absolute spectacle – a perfectly orchestrated chaos of pedestrians. I explored the trendy shops of Harajuku, got lost in the electric atmosphere of Akihabara, and found serenity in the Meiji Jingu Shrine.\n\nFrom Tokyo, I took the bullet train to Kyoto. The contrast was stunning. Kyoto felt steeped in history, with its traditional wooden machiya houses and serene gardens. I wandered through the enchanting Arashiyama Bamboo Grove, visited the iconic Fushimi Inari Shrine with its thousands of red torii gates, and learned the art of the tea ceremony.\n\nThe food was, of course, incredible. From delicate sushi to savory okonomiyaki, every meal was a delight. I embraced the local customs, attempting (and often failing!) to navigate chopsticks with grace. \n\nJapan is a country of beautiful contradictions – ancient traditions seamlessly blending with futuristic innovation. It's a place that challenges your perceptions and leaves you with a deep sense of wonder. I left feeling both exhausted and exhilarated, and already planning my return. Highly recommend adding it to your travel bucket list!\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.001122916815802455}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.1602802574634552}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -1.1920922133867862e-06}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.001033129869028926}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.1345929354429245}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.1